    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Astur</span></b> , ŭris, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. m.</i>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the province
				of Asturia</i>, <i>in</i> Hispania Tarraconensis,
				<i>Asturian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					14, 199</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">v. Asturco: exercitus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					1, 252</span></i>
			.—Subst., m., <i>an Asturian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">belliger Astur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 748</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regio Asturum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 20, 34, § 111</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conventus Asturum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					3, 4, § 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cantabri et Astures validissimae gentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 12, 46</span></i>
			 and 54.</div>
